 "news": {
  "date": "2026-09-22",
  "asof": "2026-09-23 13:19 UTC",
  "headline": "Iran offered to reopen Hormuz in seven days \u2014 and crude gave back the entire war premium",
  "standfirst": "A senior Iranian official said Tehran would reopen the Strait of Hormuz within seven days if Washington eases military pressure and lifts its blockade, an offer delivered through mediators six days earlier; Rubio said the administration was open to that, though a Trump-Pezeshkian meeting has been ruled out. WTI fell 8.6% to $89.42 \u2014 a 2.7 sigma move, below where it traded before the East-West pipeline was cut, and 14% below last Tuesday. Equities ignored it: the S&P closed exactly unchanged, the Nasdaq rose 0.45% to a new closing high, the Dow fell 0.36% and the Russell rose 0.79%. In the book OKTA rose 2.76% to 196.62, its best mark, the day before its investor summit, and GOOG holds +1.07R after a twelve-point intraday reversal. Heat 3.05R against 3.0R.",
  "themes": [
   {
    "kicker": "What's next",
    "right": "Oktane today \u00b7 Pezeshkian at the UN today",
